---
title: Tinga de Pollo
image: https://www.theanthonykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Tinga-de-Pollo-14-1365x2048.jpg
servings: 6
cuisine: Mexican
---

In a #pot{} bring @chicken stock or water{2%cups}(actual amount may vary, you need to cover the chicken) to a boil over high heat.

Add @chicken{1.5%lbs} along with seasonings to taste (i.e. @?oregano{}, @?garlic{}, @?bay leaves{}, @?salt{}, @?pepper{}, @Tajin{}, etc.). Let chicken simmer until cooked thoroughly, usually ~{12-15%minutes}.

Drain chicken and set aside.

Saute @onion{1}(small, diced) over medium-high heat in a #pan{}, then set-aside.

Heat up @salsa{2%cups}(thawed from frozen) over medium heat in a #small sauce pan{}. 

Once warm, add the sauted onions and let simmer for ~{1%minute}. Then keep warm.

Using two forks, shred the chicken into a #large mixing bowl{}.

Pour salsa/onion mixture over the chicken and mix thoroughly. Serve over rice or on warm tortillas.